    "text": "Me. ARCHIBALD NEILSON, J.P., L.R.C.P.Edin., L.F.P.S.Glasg. \r\nGlasgow. \r\nMr. Archibald Neilson, who died on 19th September, at the \r\nadvanced age of 94 years, was for a great many years a very \r\nwell known figure in the East End of Glasgow. Mr. Neilson \r\nqualified in 1865, and for many years resided at 10 Sommerville \r\nPlace, where he conducted a busy practice. He took an active \r\ninterest in municipal affairs, and sat in the Town Council for \r\nseveral years as one of the representatives of the Fourth Ward, \r\nbecoming a member of several committees in which his profes\u0002sional knowledge was valuable. He was kindly by nature, and \r\nalways ready with a word of encouragement for a junior \r\npractitioner. \n",
